# PiPerspective configuration template

Add the following block to `~/.pai/settings.json`. If you already have a
top-level object there, merge `pi_perspective` into it.

```jsonc
{
  "pi_perspective": {
    // Global kill switch. When false, all PiPerspective invocations
    // (manual and auto) return a stub verdict and spawn ZERO pi
    // subprocesses.
    "enabled": true,

    // Single model used for THINK, PLAN, and VERIFY in v1.
    // Default is openai/gpt-5-codex:high because opencode usually runs
    // a Claude-family model — out-of-family reviewer defeats groupthink.
    //
    // If opencode runs an OpenAI-family model, change this to an
    // Anthropic or Google model instead. The principle is OUT-OF-FAMILY,
    // not "always OpenAI".
    "model": "openai/gpt-5-codex:high",

    // Minimum pi --version. VersionCheck.ts asserts at startup.
    "min_pi_version": "0.73.1",

    // Effort tier -> set of phases that auto-invoke.
    // Manual invocation always works regardless of tier or kill switch
    // (well, kill switch wins; effort tier does not).
    "auto_invoke": {
      "Standard":      [],
      "Extended":      ["VERIFY"],
      "Advanced":      ["PLAN", "VERIFY"],
      "Deep":          ["THINK", "PLAN", "VERIFY"],
      "Comprehensive": ["THINK", "PLAN", "VERIFY"]
    },

    // Thinking level for VERIFY phase. Higher = more cost + latency.
    // Downshift to "medium" if your 5-run mean latency exceeds 30s.
    "verify_thinking": "high",

    // Hide blockers below this severity in the default UI summary.
    // Audit JSON always contains all blockers; this only affects display.
    "blocker_min_severity_display": "major"
  }
}
```
